hydromate.sortie / hydromate.flux_convergence
---------------------------------------------
The TELEMAC listing (".sortie") reader and the boundary-flux convergence analysis
were adopted from the `pythomac` package (https://github.com/hydro-informatics/
pythomac), lead author Sebastian Schwindt, who is also the author of hydromate and
authorised the adoption. The analysis reproduces pythomac's behaviour and writes the
same four output files (extracted-fluxes.csv, flux-convergence.png,
convergence-rate.csv, convergence-rate.png).

The implementation here is an independent one written against TELEMAC's output
format, not a copy. That is deliberate: pythomac's own listing parser
(`parser_output.py`) and its `utils/files.py` / `utils/exceptions.py` are adapted
from TELEMAC-MASCARET's `HOMETEL/scripts/python3/postel` under the GNU GPL v3 and
carry the TELEMAC-MASCARET Consortium's copyright, which is not hydromate's or
pythomac's to relicense. hydromate therefore reimplements the parsing rather than
vendoring those files, and the GAIA / tracer mass-balance field lists in
hydromate.sortie were re-derived from the FORTRAN FORMAT statements in TELEMAC
v9.1.1 (`sources/gaia/mass_balance.f`, `sources/telemac3d/bil3d.f`).

TELEMAC-MASCARET (http://www.opentelemac.org) is a separate program, invoked by
hydromate as an external solver; none of its source is included or linked here.
